-- title:
--   Integrality over A[jmath̄] from Gauss-integrality and pole-freeness
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a positive level $N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, and assume $q \nmid N$. Let $t$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$N$ modular function field (itself generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions of level $N$). Assume, first, that the Laurent series underlying $t$ lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (N * q) A.toSubring red`: writing $R$ for the subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated by the constant series with coefficients in $A$ together with the two series $j$ and $j_{N q}$, this means $t \cdot s = r$ for some $r, s \in R$ with $s$ outside the prime ideal of $R$ cut out by the reduction map built from $\mathrm{red}$. Assume, second, that for every place $u_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — that is, every valuation subring of that field which contains $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, is not the whole field and is a principal ideal ring — whose valuation ring contains `CharPModel.jBar N`, the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of $j$, the element $t$ lies in that valuation ring. The conclusion is that $t$ is integral over `CharPModel.affineBaseFin N A`, the subring of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` generated by the image of $A$ under the constants homomorphism together with `jBar N`: there is a monic polynomial $p$ over that subring with $p(t) = 0$, the evaluation being taken along the inclusion of the subring.
--
--   This is the place-wise form of Gauss's lemma for the modular function field: integrality for the Gauss prolongation of $A$ at level $Nq$ together with absence of poles at all places where $j$ is finite forces integrality over $A[\bar\jmath]$, the affine bottom ring of the finite chart. It is used in the analysis of specialisations of places of the modular function field in characteristic $q$, in particular by the lemmas on prolongation tuples governing the behaviour of residues at the cusps and at affine geometric places.
-- source:
